# Hermes Memory Provider — Environment Variables

## Required

```bash
# Postgres connection string
HERMES_MEMORY_DSN=postgres://hermes:hermesdev@localhost:5432/hermes

# AGE graph name
HERMES_MEMORY_GRAPH=hermes_knowledge
```

## Optional

```bash
# Ollama embedding endpoint (default: local Ollama)
HYBRID_AGE_EMBED_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Embedding model name (default: nomic-embed-text)
HYBRID_AGE_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# Hermes config equivalents (in config.yaml):
# hybrid_age:
#   embed_url: http://localhost:11434/v1
#   embed_model: nomic-embed-text
#   graph: hermes_knowledge
```

## Postgres Credentials

The `HERMES_MEMORY_DSN` should point to a Postgres instance with:
- `pgvector` extension installed
- `apache/age` extension installed
- Schema initialized via `example/init.sql`

Example DSN formats:
```
# Standard
postgres://hermes:hermesdev@localhost:5432/hermes

# With password containing special chars (URL-encode)
postgres://hermes:p%40ssw0rd@localhost:5432/hermes

# Remote host
postgres://hermes:hermesdev@db.example.com:5432/hermes
```
